\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces (a) Thermophysical properties of CO$_2$ at 8~MPa across the pseudo-boiling temperature $T_{pb}=307.8$~K, normalized by their values at $T_{pb}$ (computed with CoolProp~\cite  {CoolProp2014}). (b) Regenerative cooling of a liquid-rocket thrust chamber (schematic): the propellant flows at supercritical pressure through rectangular channels in the chamber wall, heated on the hot-gas side only; near the heated wall it crosses $T_{pb}$ and becomes gas-like, which can trigger heat-transfer deterioration~\cite  {Pizzarelli2018,Nasuti2021,Urbano2013}.\relax }}{4}{figure.caption.6}\protected@file@percent }
